{"agent":"apply-decisions","data":{"item":"","redactions":0,"relayed_by":"","text":"Operator 2026-11-11 answers. Workflow profile: user highest, a company floor is a default (a person-only local override may loosen it, recorded and visible); strict-delivery profile opt-in at onboarding; operator disposal of review findings by chat approval is enough; final review round = strongest reviewer on the full diff only above a size/risk threshold (configurable). Rename the new WP- tasks to WFP-. Accept all six proposed decisions: D-merge-smoke-gate, D-approval-recipe-list, D-pin-refresh-owner, D-lease-lifecycle-automation, D-phase-needs-scope, D-accepted-baseline-red. Phase needs: phase-level only unless a task opts in (needs_apply = phase default). Merge smoke gate: when a needed tool is missing record unavailable (never passed) and continue (NOT refuse). Revive the abandoned affected-tests scope as TS-impact-select gated on TS-impact-probe. Toolkit ideas to file: deviation record + citation check, commitments tier (AFTER GP-waiver lands: file it with a need on GP-waiver), readiness-audit gate, company baseline importer (patterns only, runtime import, copies nothing); also all six of: effort-adjustment rules as a layered table, one source emitted per harness, pack lint for imported skills, prose-gate recipe as documentation, a doctor view of what loads per request with a budget knob, a model-comparison log kind. The work-item (tracker) adapter folds under CP-intake and IA-forge."},"id":"e02bff752cc2cba62ab98f762","kind":"session.prompt","lamport":175878,"schema":1,"subject":"s20261111T161526-1524180","ts":"2026-11-11T16:15:27.892606Z"}
